# Audit detail — Phase {PHASE}

Flavor: `{FLAVOR}`

`SPEC.md §B` is the canonical finding ledger. This file is optional
and carries only per-finding Detail sections when a finding needs
more than a row — hypotheses, probe plans, before/after evidence.

If a finding fits inside `§B` (id, date, cause, fix) without losing
information, do not create a Detail section here.

## Status legend (for the `status`-style columns operators sometimes
add inline in §B)

- `.` open
- `~` in progress / partial
- `?` investigating
- `x` closed
- `d` deferred

## Severity scale (used in Detail headers when relevant)

- **S1** — blocks release: user-visible breakage, data loss, contracted
  invariant regression, security incident.
- **S2** — blocks phase: test/build red or behavior wrong.
- **S3** — polish: visible drift, minor a11y, naming, log noise.
- **S4** — nice-to-have: defer freely.

